{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"Security issues should be reported only to security@djangoproject.com.","source_span":"Please report security issues **only** to ``security@djangoproject.com``."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"The Django security mailing list is private, open only to long-time, highly trusted Django developers, and its archives are not public.","source_span":"This is a private list only open to long-time, highly trusted Django developers, and its archives are not public."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"The Django ticket tracker is located at https://code.djangoproject.com/.","source_span":"Before reporting a bug on the `ticket tracker <https://code.djangoproject.com/>`_"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"Issues marked \"wontfix\" should not be reopened without finding consensus to do so on the Django Forum.","source_span":"Don't reopen issues that have been marked \"wontfix\" without finding consensus to do so on the `Django Forum`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"Issues marked \"needsnewfeatureprocess\" should not be reopened without shepherding the issue through the new feature ideas GitHub project.","source_span":"Don't reopen issues that have been marked \"needsnewfeatureprocess\" without shepherding an issue through the `new feature ideas`_ GitHub project."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"Features should be proposed in the new feature ideas GitHub project by creating a new item in the Idea column, not in the ticket tracker.","source_span":"Propose the feature in the `new feature ideas`_ GitHub project (not in the ticket tracker) by creating a new item in the **Idea** column."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"A patch that changes the look or behavior of Django's UI must include before and after screenshots or screencasts.","source_span":"If you're offering a patch that changes the look or behavior of Django's UI, you **must** attach before *and* after screenshots/screencasts."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"On the new feature ideas GitHub project, emoji reactions mean: 👍 support and would use it, 👎 oppose or believe it would cause issues, 😕 no strong opinion, 🎉 straightforward and beneficial addition.","source_span":"👍: I support this feature and would use it"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"The Steering Council moves supported ideas through the stages: Idea, Approved - Idea refinement - Team creation, In progress, Working solution - Review - Feedback, Needs maintainer (Django only), Done.","source_span":"moving those with community support through the following stages"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"Informal Django Forum votes on feature ideas follow the Apache/Python style: +1, +0, -0, or -1.","source_span":"votes are given as +1, +0, -0, or -1."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"A +1 vote means \"I love the idea and I'm strongly committed to it.\"","source_span":"+1: \"I love the idea and I'm strongly committed to it.\""}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","statement":"A -1 vote means \"I strongly disagree and would be very unhappy to see the idea turn into reality.\"","source_span":"-1: \"I strongly disagree and would be very unhappy to see the idea turn into reality.\""}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[0,1],"question":"Where should security issues in Django be reported, and who has access to that list?","answer":"Only to security@djangoproject.com — a private list open only to long-time, highly trusted Django developers, and its archives are not public."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What must happen before reopening a Django ticket that's been marked \"wontfix\"?","answer":"Consensus to reopen it must be found on the Django Forum."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What's required before reopening a ticket marked \"needsnewfeatureprocess\"?","answer":"The issue must be shepherded through the new feature ideas GitHub project."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What extra requirement applies to a patch that changes the look or behavior of Django's UI?","answer":"It must include both before and after screenshots or screencasts."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What do the four emoji reactions mean on Django's new feature ideas GitHub project?","answer":"👍 means support and would use it, 👎 means opposition, 😕 means no strong opinion, and 🎉 means it seems like a straightforward and beneficial addition."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_bugs-and-features","fact_refs":[9,10],"question":"What informal voting scale is used in Django Forum discussions, and what does a +1 vote mean?","answer":"Votes are given as +1, +0, -0, or -1; a +1 means \"I love the idea and I'm strongly committed to it.\""}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Since Django is hosted on GitHub, patches are provided in the form of pull requests.","source_span":"Since Django is hosted on GitHub, patches are provided in the form of pull requests."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"A git alias `pr = !sh -c \"git fetch upstream pull/${1}/head:pr/${1} && git checkout pr/${1}\"` added to ~/.gitconfig lets you run `git pr ####` to check out a pull request.","source_span":"pr = !sh -c \\\"git fetch upstream pull/${1}/head:pr/${1} && git checkout pr/${1}\\\""}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Mergers use `git rebase -i` and `git commit --amend` to bring commits up to the expected quality level.","source_span":"Use ``git rebase -i`` and ``git commit --amend`` to make sure the commits have the expected level of quality."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Work is merged to main as a \"fast-forward\" (via git merge --ff-only) to avoid a merge commit.","source_span":"Merge the work as \"fast-forward\" to main to avoid a merge commit."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Force pushing to the pull request branch after rebasing on main but before merging makes the commit hashes on main and the branch match, which automatically closes the pull request.","source_span":"Force push to the branch after rebasing on main but before merging and pushing to upstream. This allows the commit hashes on main and the branch to match which automatically closes the pull request."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"If a pull request doesn't need to be merged as multiple commits, GitHub's \"Squash and merge\" button can be used instead.","source_span":"If a pull request doesn't need to be merged as multiple commits, you can use GitHub's \"Squash and merge\" button on the website."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"The published history of django/django branches must never be changed by force pushing, except in cases like security reasons, and only after discussing the situation with the team.","source_span":"Never change the published history of ``django/django`` branches by force pushing. If you absolutely must (for security reasons for example), first discuss the situation with the team."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Commit messages must be written in the past tense, with the subject line ending in a period, e.g. \"Fixed Unicode bug in RSS API.\"","source_span":"Write detailed commit messages in the past tense, not present tense, and end the subject line with a period.\n\n  * Correct: \"Fixed Unicode bug in RSS API.\""}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Commit messages should use lines of 72 characters maximum.","source_span":"The commit message should be in lines of 72 chars maximum."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Contributors should be credited in commit messages, e.g. \"Thanks A for the report and B for review,\" using git's Co-Authored-By as appropriate.","source_span":"Credit the contributors in the commit message: \"Thanks A for the report and B for review.\" Use git's `Co-Authored-By`_ as appropriate"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Commits should be limited to the most granular change that makes sense, favoring frequent small commits over infrequent large ones.","source_span":"Limit commits to the most granular change that makes sense. This means, use frequent small commits rather than infrequent large commits."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","statement":"Bug fixes should be separated from feature changes, since bugfixes may need to be backported.","source_span":"Separate bug fixes from feature changes. Bugfixes may need to be :ref:`backported"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[0],"question":"How are code contributions to Django submitted, given that it's hosted on GitHub?","answer":"Patches are provided in the form of pull requests."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What git alias lets a Django merger check out a pull request locally by its number, and how is it used?","answer":"Adding `pr = !sh -c \"git fetch upstream pull/${1}/head:pr/${1} && git checkout pr/${1}\"` to ~/.gitconfig lets you run `git pr ####` to check out the corresponding pull request."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Why do Django mergers force-push to a pull request's branch after rebasing but before merging to upstream?","answer":"So the commit hashes on main and the branch match, which automatically closes the pull request."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What tense and punctuation rule applies to the subject line of a Django commit message, with an example?","answer":"It must be written in the past tense and end with a period, e.g. \"Fixed Unicode bug in RSS API.\""}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What is the maximum line length for a Django commit message?","answer":"72 characters maximum."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_committing-code","fact_refs":[6],"question":"When, if ever, is it acceptable to force-push and change the published history of django/django branches?","answer":"Only in exceptional cases such as security reasons, and only after first discussing the situation with the team."}
